  {
    "node": 2,
    "tag": "para",
    "id": "fs-id1170655163394",
    "field": "text",
    "source": "In the last section, we listed many operation symbols that are used in algebra, then we translated expressions and equations into English phrases and sentences. Now we’ll reverse the process. We’ll translate English phrases into algebraic expressions. The symbols and variables we’ve talked about will help us do that."
  },
  {
    "node": 3,
    "tag": "link",
    "id": null,
    "field": "tail",
    "source": "summarizes them."
  },
  {
    "node": 4,
    "tag": "table",
    "id": "fs-id1170655166578",
    "field": "@aria-label",
    "source": "This table has five rows and three columns. The first row is a header row and it labels each column. The first column is labeled \"Operation\", the second \"Phrase\" and the last \"Expression\". The next row has the word addition in the \"Operation\" column. In the \"Phrase\" column is a list of phrases: a plus b, the sum of a and b, a increased by b, b more than a, the total of a and b, and b added to a. In the \"Expression\" column is the expression a, plus sign, b. The next row has the word subtraction in the \"Operation\" column. In the \"Phrase\" column is a list of phrases: a minus b, the difference of a and b, a decreased by b, b less than a, and b subtracted from a. In the \"Expression\" column is the expression a, minus sign, b. The next row has the word multiplication in the \"Operation\" column. In the \"Phrase\" column is a list of phrases: a times b, the product of a and b, and twice a. In the \"Expression\" column are a list of expressions: a, dot multiplication sign, b; a and b; a and b in parentheses; and a in parentheses and b in parentheses. Below this list is the expression 2a which represents the phrase twice a. The last row has the word division in the \"Operation\" column. In the \"Phrase\" column is a list of phrases: a divided by b, the quotient of a and b, the ratio of a and b, and b divided into a. In the \"Expression\" column are a list of expressions: a, division sign, b; a, slash, b; a above the fraction bar and b below the fraction bar; and b outside the division bracket and a inside the division bracket."
  },
